  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14269080/assets/abafb7d55b4baa0b06f20c3de2b44d5925f7286f078aaa76d71aded7c9c9a001.png)\n\nNow, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the domain of $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is false since $f(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\n- Statement III is false since $f(-1)=\\sqrt[3]{-1}=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
